            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery-left ventricular fistula and multiple ventricular septal defects due to blunt chest trauma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1055-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 27 year old man developed multiple ventricular septal defects and a coronary artery ventricular fistula after a blunt injury. These were treated successfully by surgery, which was carried out four months after the injury to allow some healing of the defect to occur.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
